Description: U235 is a special nuclear material.  It is the form of uranium that is enriched for both fuel and military use, and as a result HEU will be reported as U235.
# TBD
# Relative intensity of 97/186 should higher for U238, lower for U235
# There is no-609 line so Bi214 daughter/contam daughter doesn't seem possible
# *but* no other obvious explantion for 1113, 1762, 2116 lines.  Maybe Bi207?
# Purified HEU contains approx 0.03% U234, 3.5% U235, and 96.47% U238
# Within a few days, U235 establishes equilibrium with Th231.
# Within a few months, U238 establishes equilibirum with Th234 and Pa234m.
# U234 takes a long time to evolve stable Th230 quantities.

# Don't really like eliminating the 97/186-only template, since that
# was a legal combination in our old idtree.  However, it does not
# seem necessary since at least one of the other higher lines always
# show up, while having the-97 line shielded is extremely common.
